<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Synthetics jumps 11.37 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Synthetics jumps 11.37 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Synthetics jumped 1.20 rupees, or 11.37 percent, to 11.75 on Tuesday on expectations that manufacturers will increase polyester staple fibre (PSF) prices next month, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 15,000 shares of the stock had changed hands by midsession.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not just Pak Synthetics, but the entire sector is up as manufacturers are expected to increase PSF rates at their quarterly meeting in November,&quot; dealer Sajjad Mankani said.</p>
<p>The manufacturers review PSF prices every three months.</p>
<p>Mankani said last week's rupee devaluation would help local manufacturers as imported fibre would cost more.</p>
<p>-- Amir Zia 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
